---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The executive layer for AI"
  description="Obedience Corp is researching organized diffusion: systems aimed at turning vague user intent into expected results with minimal intervention between input and outcome."
>
  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Hero — company-level positioning for organized diffusion.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-head">
        <p class="mono-label hero-eyebrow">Organized diffusion</p>
        <h1 class="hero-h1">
          The executive<br />layer for AI.
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-body">
        <p>
          AI can do more work than ever. The limiting factor is keeping that work coherent. Obedience is the executive layer for AI: organized diffusion that carries your intent into structured, verifiable execution across agents, tools, and context.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-audience mono-label">For founders and teams directing complex work with AI</p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href="#system" class="hero-cta hero-cta-primary">See the system <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <a href="#contact" class="hero-cta">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       System in practice — a concrete, illustrative example of how
       intent moves through the released Festival workflow layer.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="system" class="system">
    <div class="system-inner">
      <div class="system-intro">
        <p class="mono-label system-eyebrow">The system in practice</p>
        <h2 class="system-h2">Intent becomes a sequence the system can carry.</h2>
        <p class="system-lede">
          Festival is the first released layer of the stack. It turns a goal into structured work, preserves the state between sessions, and gives the human director a legible place to intervene.
        </p>
      </div>

      <article class="system-example" aria-labelledby="system-example-title">
        <div class="system-example-header">
          <span id="system-example-title" class="mono-label">Example / Product launch</span>
          <span class="mono-label">State / In progress</span>
        </div>

        <ol class="system-steps">
          <li class="system-step">
            <span class="system-step-index">01</span>
            <div>
              <p class="mono-label">Intent</p>
              <h3>Ship a public launch</h3>
              <p>Turn a strategic outcome into a shared direction the system can preserve.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="system-step">
            <span class="system-step-index">02</span>
            <div>
              <p class="mono-label">Structure</p>
              <h3>Define phases, sequences, and tasks</h3>
              <p>Make ownership, dependencies, and the next useful action explicit.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="system-step">
            <span class="system-step-index">03</span>
            <div>
              <p class="mono-label">Execution</p>
              <h3>Continue across sessions and tools</h3>
              <p>Let agents work within the plan without rebuilding the project state each time.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="system-step">
            <span class="system-step-index">04</span>
            <div>
              <p class="mono-label">Verification</p>
              <h3>Review the outcome and decide what is next</h3>
              <p>Keep evidence and judgment in the loop as the work resolves.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="system-example-footer">
          <span class="mono-label">Illustrative flow · Festival is available now</span>
          <a href="/work" class="system-link">Explore Festival <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <figure class="system-demo">
        <img
          src="/images/demos/tui-delegate.gif"
          alt="Terminal capture of Festival's interface: a plain-language intent for a new app is typed in and delegated to an agent, which turns it into structured work."
          width="860"
          height="556"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="mono-label">
          Real capture · an intent delegated through Festival's terminal interface
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Thesis section — continuation of the narrative, copy from the
       user's Landing Page Version. Honest about shipping status.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="thesis" class="thesis">
    <div class="thesis-inner">
      <p class="mono-label thesis-eyebrow">The Shift</p>

      <article class="thesis-body">
        <p>The advances in AI so far have been advances in prediction. Language models predict text, image models predict pixels, and both can produce something that looks right. Organized diffusion is the layer that produces something that <em>is</em> right: you give it your intent, and it carries that intent across your agents, tools, and context, staying with the work until the outcome is done or proven impossible.</p>

        <h2>Today you’re the connective tissue</h2>
        <p>AI agent harnesses do real work. They call tools, build things, search the web, write code, manipulate files. What they can’t do is reach the final outcome on their own. They run a few steps, stop, and hand control back. You review, redirect, kick off another loop. The work happens in fragments, and you are the connective tissue between every fragment.</p>
        <p>The gap isn’t that AI can’t do the work. It’s that today’s systems can’t sustain themselves through it. They need you to supply the structure, the judgment, the next step, every time.</p>

        <h2>What changes with organized diffusion</h2>
        <p>A well-run company doesn’t work by the CEO talking to every person doing every task. It works because the systems and processes around them let competent people succeed in their roles without constant oversight and messages. The CEO supplies intent and strategy. The organization runs.</p>
        <p>You can approximate that today by wiring agent harnesses into the shape of a human organization. But at scale the seams show: more points of failure, and far more information than one person can absorb.</p>
        <p>Organized diffusion is that operating layer: it standardizes how work is organized, abstracts progress into a form a human can understand, trust, and audit, and lets that structure compound through normal usage.</p>

        <h2>User-owned by design</h2>
        <p>Your data, your context, and your history belong to you. They should be portable by default, easy to inspect, and easy to move. You shouldn’t have to fight to export your own information or rebuild your setup every time a tool changes direction.</p>
        <p>And because your information stays yours, you stay free to use whatever AI models and tools serve you best. New tools should plug into your data, not lock you into someone else’s platform.</p>

        <h2>Why this matters</h2>
        <p>Imagine if you woke up tomorrow and your baseline productivity increased by 10x. Within a few weeks you would adjust to the new normal. Now imagine it increased 5,000x, or 100,000x. What would you do with that capacity? How would you reason about work happening at that scale to even know the system is working?</p>
        <p>Throughout history, that kind of productive leverage has belonged to a few people at the top: CEOs of large companies, politicians, heads of institutions. As AI gets more capable and cheaper, it becomes affordable to a far wider pool of people. But very few people have experience directing effort at that scale, and the systems we use to organize work were designed for a world that no longer exists.</p>
        <p>The barrier to this scale of capability is not training a better LLM. It is making everything produced by the AI legible, verifiable, and useful at scale, without mentally overwhelming the human director. And that's what organized diffusion enables us to build.</p>

        <p class="thesis-more">
          <a href="/thesis">Read the full thesis <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>The people who can direct and verify work at scale will outperform the people who supervise it one conversation at a time.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <p class="founder-note-trigger">
          <button type="button" id="founder-note-open" class="founder-note-link">
            Founder's note <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </button>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Founder's note — modal dialog. Triggered from the thesis section.
       Native <dialog> with ESC to close, click-outside to dismiss.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <dialog id="founder-note" class="founder-note-dialog" aria-labelledby="founder-note-title">
    <div class="founder-note-content">
      <button
        type="button"
        id="founder-note-close"
        class="founder-note-close"
        aria-label="Close founder's note"
      >
        <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
      </button>

      <p class="mono-label founder-note-eyebrow">Founder's note</p>
      <h2 id="founder-note-title" class="founder-note-title">Where I am today</h2>

      <div class="founder-note-body">
        <p>I've been working on this system as a solo founder since early 2025, and I've been dogfooding it since May 2025. I've built more with this system in the past year than every team I've been on in my 11 years working in software, both in breadth and depth. I am completely reliant on my system because there is no viable alternative that can handle the workload that's now become normal to me.</p>
        <p>Festival is already released at <a href="https://fest.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">fest.build</a>. What's missing now is packaging, positioning, and financing for the rest of the stack. Today I use the system to build complex products and set up automated coding or research pipelines that require a level of specification and reliability that can't be done with ordinary agent loops.</p>
        <p>I'm building this regardless. Investment changes the speed, not the direction: with backing, the focus goes to productization, marketing, and demonstrations. Without it, the stack keeps growing the way it has so far, through daily use on real work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Contact section — form copied verbatim from the previous
       src/pages/contact.astro (which is deleted in Task 8).
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="contact" class="contact">
    <div class="contact-inner">
      <h2 class="contact-h2">Direct more ambitious work.</h2>
      <p class="contact-intro">
        If you're building with AI at a scale that ordinary prompts and task boards can't support, reach out for early access to Obedience, a Festival demo, investment, or partnership.
      </p>

      <form
        id="contact-form"
        action="https://formspree.io/f/xgopdrej"
        method="POST"
        class="contact-form"
      >
        <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />

        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="name" class="mono-label">Name</label>
          <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required placeholder="Your name" />
        </div>

        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="email" class="mono-label">Email</label>
          <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </div>

        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="message" class="mono-label">Message</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" required rows="5" placeholder="Tell us what you're interested in..."></textarea>
        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="submit-btn mono-label">
          Send message <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </button>

        <p id="form-status" class="form-status"></p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    min-height: 100vh;
    min-height: 100svh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-inner {
    flex: 1;
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 6vh, 5rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    column-gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    row-gap: clamp(2rem, 4vh, 3rem);
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .hero-inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: end;
    }
    .hero-head { grid-column: 1 / 2; }
    .hero-body { grid-column: 2 / 3; margin: 0; }
    .hero-ctas { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  }

  .hero-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .hero-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 9vw, 10rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 3rem;
  }

  .hero-body {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 2rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .hero-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.15vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-body);
    margin: 0 0 1.25em;
  }

  .hero-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .hero-audience {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .hero-ctas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .hero-cta {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 2.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-primary);
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: background-color 200ms ease, color 200ms ease,
      transform 200ms ease, box-shadow 200ms ease;
    will-change: transform;
  }

  .hero-cta > span {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 220ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  }

  .hero-cta:hover {
    background: var(--color-ink-primary);
    color: var(--color-bg-primary);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 24px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
  }

  .hero-cta:active {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  .hero-cta:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-ink-primary);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Secondary "See the work →" — arrow slides right on hover */
  .hero-cta:not(.hero-cta-primary):hover > span {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  .hero-cta-primary {
    background: var(--color-ink-primary);
    color: var(--color-bg-primary);
  }

  .hero-cta-primary:hover {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  /* Primary "Read more ↓" — arrow nudges down on hover */
  .hero-cta-primary:hover > span {
    transform: translateY(3px);
  }

  /* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     System in practice
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .system {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .system-inner {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 9vh, 7rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .system-intro {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vh, 4.5rem);
  }

  .system-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .system-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.03;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    max-width: 15ch;
  }

  .system-lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 54ch;
  }

  .system-example {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  }

  .system-example-header,
  .system-example-footer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .system-example-header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .system-example-footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .system-steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .system-step {
    min-height: 18rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .system-step:last-child {
    border-right: none;
  }

  .system-step-index {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .system-step .mono-label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }

  .system-step h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }

  .system-step p:last-child {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .system-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .system-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .system-demo {
    margin: clamp(2rem, 5vh, 3.5rem) auto 0;
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .system-demo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  }

  .system-demo figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Thesis section
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .thesis {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .thesis-inner {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 9vh, 7rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .thesis-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .thesis-body {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink-body);
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .thesis-body > p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5em;
  }

  .thesis-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.75vw, 1.375rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .thesis-body ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.75em;
  }

  .thesis-body ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.75em;
    margin-bottom: 0.25em;
  }

  .thesis-body ul li::before {
    content: "·";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.25em;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .thesis-body strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .thesis-more {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }

  .thesis-more a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .thesis-more a:hover {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .thesis-body blockquote {
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .thesis-body blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 32ch;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  /* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Contact section
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .contact-inner {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 9vh, 7rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .contact-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .contact-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin: 0 0 clamp(2rem, 4vh, 3rem);
  }

  .contact-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .form-field label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .form-field input,
  .form-field textarea {
    width: 100%;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding: 0.65rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    outline: none;
    transition: border-color 150ms ease;
    resize: none;
  }

  .form-field input::placeholder,
  .form-field textarea::placeholder {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .form-field input:focus,
  .form-field textarea:focus {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .submit-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ink-primary);
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: opacity 150ms ease;
  }

  .submit-btn:hover {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .form-status {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    min-height: 1.5em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .form-status[data-state="ok"] {
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .form-status[data-state="err"] {
    color: #b84a3d;
  }

  /* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Founder's note — trigger + modal dialog
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .founder-note-trigger {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .founder-note-link {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
